<title>GREECE: SCHEDULE ON GREEK CORPORATE BRIEFING.</title>
<headline>SCHEDULE ON GREEK CORPORATE BRIEFING.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corporate briefing of Greek</p>
<p>institutional investors goes ahead with construction firm AEGEK</p>
<p>and information technology listing Pouliadis </p>
<p>on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The presentations are part of regular briefings over</p>
<p>fundamentals and business plans of listed Greek companies held</p>
<p>on a weekly basis.</p>
<p>A total of 44 Greek listed companies has come under the</p>
<p>scrutiny of Greek institutional investors since Dec 18, 1996.</p>
<p>Around 30 more are slated for a presentation in the coming</p>
<p>months.</p>
<p>The schedule for the coming weeks is as follows:</p>
<p>May 21, 1997	AEGEK SA </p>
<p>			Pouliadis SA </p>
<p>May 28, 1997	Themeliodomi SA </p>
<p>			Loulis Flour Mills SA </p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301-3311812-4</p>
</text>
